-- regenerate it with ./gradlew generate rather than editing it.

---A `ObjType` config contains the descriptive data necessary for the game to populate a `ObjStackEntity`.
---
---These config types can be found within the `config.Obj` table:
---
---Info: An `ObjType` is a Proxy usertype, which means it is safe to copy and store in your scripts. It cannot, however,
---be used with any persistent storage.
---
---Information available within an `ObjType` includes:
---@class ObjType
---@field id integer (Read-only) The ID of this config type.
---@field configName string (Read-only) The name of this config, i.e. `"STEEL_BAR"`.
---@field typeName string (Read-only) The type of this config. Will always be `"Obj"`.
---@field name string (Read-only) The display name of this config type.
---@field isMembers boolean (Read-only) Whether this object is for members.
---@field category integer (Read-only) The category type of this config. Returns `-1` if none is set. Category name is available using `id.Category.FromID()`.
---@field teamID integer (Read-only) Assigns this team ID to a PlayerEntity if the object is worn.
---@field cost Long (Read-only) The 64-bit numeric value of this object.
---@field stackType ObjStackType (Read-only) The stacking behaviour of this config.
---@field isStockmarket boolean (Read-only) Whether this object can be traded on the Grand Exchange.
---@field stockmarketBuyLimit integer (Read-only) How many of this item can be bought on the Grand Exchage during a 4-hour period.
---@field isTradeable boolean (Read-only) Whether the object can be traded between players and to shops.
---@field quests QuestTypeConfig[] (Read-only) A list of all quests related to this config.
---@field groundOpNames table<integer, string> (Read-only) A list of names displayed for the available ops when the object is shown on the ground. Use `pairs()` to iterate this list, which will provide both the op index and name as `opIndex,opName`.
---@field interfaceOpNames table<integer, string> (Read-only) A list of names displayed for the available ops when the object is shown in an interface component. Use `pairs()` to iterate this list, which will provide both the op index and name as `opIndex,opName`.
---@field stackCountAltObjs [integer, ObjType][] (Read-only) A list of `[ count, config ]` pairs used to select which `ObjType` config is used to draw the current object. The list is iterated over, and selected the last pair the input `count` was `>=` to. This list will be empty if there are no alt configs.
---@field params ParamType[] (Read-only) Returns a list of all the ParamTypes stored in this config.
---@field paramCount integer (Read-only) How many params this config has.
---@field isValid boolean (Read-only) Whether this config is valid.
local ObjType = {}

